---
import DefaultPageLayout from "../../layouts/DefaultPageLayout.astro";
import Petapetual from "../../components/Petapetual.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
---

<DefaultPageLayout
    title="Late Relatives"
    description="Navigating the loss of a family member is difficult. Learn how to pay respects and honor their memory. Petapetual offers a peaceful space to build a lasting online tribute."
>
    <article class="article-container">
        <a href="/examples" class="back-link">
            <i class="fas fa-arrow-left"></i> All Use Cases
        </a>

        <Image
            src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1559734840-f9509ee5677f?ixlib=rb-4.1.0&ixid=M3wxMjA3fDB8MHxwaG90by1wYWdlfHx8fGVufDB8fHx8fA%3D%3D&auto=format&fit=crop&q=80&w=987"
            alt="Bonded by blood but inseparable by fate- create a Petapetual online memorial to honor them today."
            class="article-hero"
            width="987"
            height="400"
        />

        <h1 class="article-title">
            <Petapetual /> for dearly departed relatives
        </h1>

        <p class="article-text">
            There's truly no easy way to navigate the loss of family members.
            It's a deeply personal, profound, and tremendously emotional
            experience that can leave you feeling adrift. The world feels
            quieter, and the space they once filled feels impossibly large.
        </p>

        <p class="article-text">
            In the midst of that sorrow, a powerful need often surfaces: the
            desire to remember them, honor them, and pay respects to them. We
            find ourselves wanting to gather the fragments of their life, the
            happy memories, the funny stories, and the photos that capture their
            smile <em>just right</em>. We want to celebrate the beautiful,
            complex life they lived.
        </p>

        <p class="article-text">
            This is a fundamental part of grieving and remembering. It's the
            need for a place to put that love and a way to share it with others
            who are also feeling the loss.
        </p>

        <p class="article-text">
            At <Petapetual />, we understand that need deeply. We created our
            online memorials to offer a peaceful, permanent space where you can
            build a beautiful tribute to your loved one. It's a place to collect
            those cherished photos, write down those precious stories, and
            invite family and friends from all over the world to share their own
            memories. It allows their light to keep shining and provides a
            central place for comfort, reflection, and celebration, ensuring
            their legacy is preserved for generations to come.
        </p>

        <div class="article-cta">
            <a href="https://app.petapetual.com" class="cta-btn">
                Create a Memorial <i class="fas fa-arrow-right ml-1"></i>
            </a>
        </div>
    </article>
</DefaultPageLayout>

<style>
    @reference "tailwindcss";

    .article-container {
        @apply flex flex-col gap-6;
    }

    .back-link {
        @apply text-sm no-underline transition-colors;
        color: var(--color-pp-mid);
    }

    .back-link:hover {
        color: var(--color-pp-primary);
    }

    .article-hero {
        @apply w-full h-48 object-cover rounded-xl shadow-sm;
        @apply lg:h-72;
    }

    .article-title {
        @apply text-2xl font-bold;
        @apply lg:text-3xl;
        color: var(--color-pp-primary);
    }

    .article-subtitle {
        @apply text-xl font-semibold mt-4;
        color: var(--color-pp-primary);
    }

    .article-text {
        @apply leading-relaxed;
        color: var(--color-pp-dark);
    }

    .article-cta {
        @apply mt-4 py-8 text-center;
        border-top: 1px solid
            color-mix(in srgb, var(--color-pp-mid) 30%, transparent);
    }

    .cta-btn {
        @apply inline-block px-6 py-3 rounded-lg font-semibold no-underline transition-colors;
        background-color: var(--color-pp-primary);
        color: var(--color-pp-light);
    }

    .cta-btn:hover {
        opacity: 0.9;
    }
</style>
